WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.843
This video shows how to move a VMware virtual machine

2
00:00:03.843 --> 00:00:07.347
to OpenShift Virtualization with a cold migration.

3
00:00:07.347 --> 00:00:11.369
A cold migration copies the virtual machine while it is shut down.

4
00:00:11.369 --> 00:00:15.373
We use Migration for Virtualization in the OpenShift web console,

5
00:00:15.373 --> 00:00:17.591
and the lab's vCenter as the source.

6
00:00:18.791 --> 00:00:22.088
Before we start, here is what the migration connects.

7
00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:27.210
On the left is VMware Cloud Foundation, on IBM Cloud Classic Infrastructure.

8
00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:33.607
Our source virtual machine sits in the lab-4399 folder, and vCenter manages it.

9
00:00:33.607 --> 00:00:38.929
On the right is Red Hat OpenShift Virtualization, on an IBM Cloud VPC.

10
00:00:38.929 --> 00:00:41.776
A transit gateway joins the two sides.

11
00:00:41.776 --> 00:00:45.047
Migration Toolkit for Virtualization, on OpenShift,

12
00:00:45.047 --> 00:00:48.924
connects to vCenter through its provider configuration.

13
00:00:48.924 --> 00:00:53.971
A network mapping sends the source network to a Localnet network on OpenShift.

14
00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:58.843
A storage mapping sends the source datastore to OpenShift Data Foundation.

15
00:00:58.843 --> 00:01:03.590
Then the migration plan moves the machine, and virt-v2v converts its disk.

16
00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:05.710
Once migrated,

17
00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:10.987
the machine joins a shared Localnet network called lab-common, on VLAN 500.

18
00:01:10.987 --> 00:01:18.582
This network reaches a dedicated subnet of the VPC for migrated machines,

19
00:01:18.582 --> 00:01:20.284
10.26.6.0/24.

20
00:01:20.284 --> 00:01:24.906
Every lab has its own project, and all of them use this one shared network.

21
00:01:24.906 --> 00:01:29.628
Each machine needs a virtual network interface, or VNI, in that subnet.

22
00:01:29.628 --> 00:01:31.775
The lab team already made them for you.

23
00:01:32.975 --> 00:01:36.772
We start in the OpenShift web console, in our lab project.

24
00:01:36.772 --> 00:01:40.869
We open Migration for Virtualization, and click Network maps.

25
00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:45.316
A network map says which target network each source network joins.

26
00:01:45.316 --> 00:01:48.738
We click Create network map, then Create with form.

27
00:01:48.738 --> 00:01:51.610
We name it lab39-networkmap.

28
00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:57.008
We choose the source provider ocp-gym-vc and the target provider host.

29
00:01:57.008 --> 00:01:59.778
For the networks, we choose the lab's source segment,

30
00:01:59.778 --> 00:02:01.905
and the shared lab-common network.

31
00:02:01.905 --> 00:02:03.027
We click Create.

32
00:02:09.916 --> 00:02:12.038
Next we make a storage map.

33
00:02:12.038 --> 00:02:16.285
It says which target storage class each source datastore uses.

34
00:02:16.285 --> 00:02:20.932
We open Storage maps, click Create storage map, then Create with form.

35
00:02:20.932 --> 00:02:23.679
We name it lab39-storagemap.

36
00:02:23.679 --> 00:02:26.151
The providers are the same as before.

37
00:02:26.151 --> 00:02:28.787
We choose the lab's source datastore,

38
00:02:28.787 --> 00:02:33.198
and the target storage class ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd.

39
00:02:33.198 --> 00:02:37.446
This is the OpenShift Data Foundation class for virtual machine disks.

40
00:02:37.446 --> 00:02:38.568
We click Create.

41
00:02:43.398 --> 00:02:45.045
Now we make the plan.

42
00:02:45.045 --> 00:02:48.342
We open Migration plans and click Create plan.

43
00:02:48.342 --> 00:02:50.789
The wizard opens on the General step.

44
00:02:50.789 --> 00:02:54.111
We name the plan cold-migration-lab39.

45
00:02:54.111 --> 00:02:56.833
The plan project is our lab project.

46
00:02:56.833 --> 00:03:02.231
We choose the source provider ocp-gym-vc and the target provider host.

47
00:03:02.231 --> 00:03:06.053
We choose our lab project as the target project, and click Next.

48
00:03:10.779 --> 00:03:14.001
On the Virtual machines step, we choose what to move.

49
00:03:14.001 --> 00:03:16.823
The tree lists the lab's source machines.

50
00:03:16.823 --> 00:03:21.095
We type lab-39 in the filter, so only our own machine is left.

51
00:03:21.095 --> 00:03:25.817
We expand the lab-4399 folder, and tick lab-39.

52
00:03:25.817 --> 00:03:27.714
Its power state is On.

53
00:03:27.714 --> 00:03:28.662
We click Next.

54
00:03:32.433 --> 00:03:35.555
The Network map step offers an existing map.

55
00:03:35.555 --> 00:03:39.302
We keep that choice, and select lab39-networkmap.

56
00:03:39.302 --> 00:03:40.599
We click Next.

57
00:03:40.599 --> 00:03:43.421
The Storage map step works the same way.

58
00:03:43.421 --> 00:03:46.668
We select lab39-storagemap, and click Next.

59
00:03:51.608 --> 00:03:55.355
On the Migration type step, we select Cold migration.

60
00:03:55.355 --> 00:04:00.002
A cold migration shuts the virtual machine down before it copies the disks.

61
00:04:00.002 --> 00:04:01.924
We click Skip to review.

62
00:04:01.924 --> 00:04:04.521
We check the summary, and click Create plan.

63
00:04:11.032 --> 00:04:12.854
The plan page opens.

64
00:04:12.854 --> 00:04:16.476
The plan checks itself first, and nothing has moved yet.

65
00:04:16.476 --> 00:04:18.698
We click Start to begin the migration.

66
00:04:22.559 --> 00:04:25.081
We open the Virtual machines tab.

67
00:04:25.081 --> 00:04:27.403
Here we can follow the migration.

68
00:04:27.403 --> 00:04:31.600
The status is Running, and the disk transfer counts the megabytes copied.

69
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.722
This takes about five minutes, so we skip ahead.

70
00:04:34.722 --> 00:04:36.669
The status is now Succeeded.

71
00:04:38.088 --> 00:04:41.635
Last, we open Virtualization and VirtualMachines.

72
00:04:41.635 --> 00:04:46.382
Our machine, lab-39, now runs on OpenShift in our lab project.

73
00:04:46.382 --> 00:04:49.204
It started as a VMware virtual machine.

74
00:04:50.405 --> 00:04:55.002
You moved a VMware virtual machine to OpenShift with a cold migration.

75
00:04:55.002 --> 00:04:57.499
Next, try a warm migration.

76
00:04:57.499 --> 00:05:00.771
It keeps the source machine running while it copies the disks.

